tils_sql_analysis.py`, `tests/test_docs.py` and `tests/test_permissions.py`; all 228 passed (3 xpassed, 140 subtests passed).\n\nChanges, per the spec:\n- **`datasette/default_actions.py`**: added `create-view` (`cv`, on the database) after `create-table`, and `drop-view` (`dv`, on the table resource) after `drop-table`.\n- **`datasette/write_sql.py`**: `create` on a `view` requires `create-view` on the database, and `drop` on a `view` requires `drop-view` on the view's table resource. `create` on a view with no database stays unsupported, as the spec asks.\n- **`datasette/utils/sql_analysis.py`**: renamed `dropped_tables` to `dropped_tables_and_views` and added views to it, so the spurious `delete` SQLite reports for a dropped view no longer becomes a `delete-row` requirement.\n- **`docs/authentication.rst`**: added both actions to the `--root` list and added `create-view` and `drop-view` sections with the anchors the spec gives.\n\nI left `SPEC.md` untracked and did not commit anything.", "ttft_ms": 1282, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 35907, "uuid": "fb93cbcb-b0c3-45da-a5b3-289e9b6225a1", "ttft_stream_ms": 958, "time_to_request_ms": 273, "first_content_frame_ms": 958, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
